Apple today <a href="https://www.apple.com/mz/newsroom/2026/09/icloud-plus-expands-to-include-apple-tv-and-apple-arcade/">announced</a> a new subscription initiative that turns paid iCloud+ subscriptions into a broader services bundle in more than 100 countries. <br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/Apple-iCloud-Plus-expansion-hero-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="2560" height="1707" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065058" /><br/>
In select countries, Apple says every paid iCloud+ plan, including the cheapest 50GB tier, now includes Apple TV and Apple Arcade "at no additional cost," while family sharing extends the storage, TV and Arcade access to up to five people.<br/>
<br/>
The initiative does not include the U.S., Canada, Australia, the UK, and European markets, but it is clearly more than a promotional offer, since Apple TV and Apple Arcade will stop being sold as individual subscriptions through Apple in countries where it has launched. Apple says existing standalone subscriptions will be cancelled as customers transition to access through iCloud+, while Arcade saves and progress are preserved. <br/>
<br/>
